 **Reason:** under a fixed common observation grid, the nuisance term \(g_m=\log(\Delta/\bar T_m)\) is structurally near-collinear with a monotone rate modifier because both are functions of the same scalar timescale. The original S0.6 simultaneously required VIF > 5 to return NOT IDENTIFIABLE and required an adjusted \(\beta_1\) estimate compatible with zero. These requirements cannot both be satisfied in the fixed-grid case.  
 **Change:** S0.6 is split into S0.6a (fixed-grid identifiability stress test; correct outcome may be NOT IDENTIFIABLE) and S0.6b (heterogeneous-grid adjustment validation; adjusted false-positive behavior is evaluated only when VIF ≤ 5). §16 is updated so that this synthetic engineering preflight precedes the formal freeze, while the unchanged code must be rerun after freeze before biological data analysis.  
 **Effect on scientific hypotheses:** none. No inclusion criterion, biological estimand, success criterion for P1–P3, or biological dataset was changed.
